{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0166T8kmbA7e6cnHEuUcpe9W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have the full paper and the review context. Let me organize my understanding before dispatching the two reviewers.\n\n**Paper Summary:**\n- Title: \"Structural Self-Consistency for Quality Estimation in LLM-Based Information Extraction\"\n- Compares 5 unsupervised confidence signals (log-probability, exact match, Fleiss' κ, Soft Jaccard, entity voting) for quality estimation and sample selection in LLM-based IE (NER and RE)\n- 2 models (Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B), 2 datasets (SciERC, CoNLL-2003), plus OOD eval on WNUT-2017\n\n\n- The key findings show that structural consistency methods like voting and Soft Jaccard outperform simpler signals, but there's a disconnect between quality estimation and effective sample selection, with performance degrading significantly on relation extraction due to cascading errors.\n\n- The experiments I've outlined are all represented in the paper across multiple tables and appendices, so I'm ready to move forward with the review process.\n\n- I'm setting up two parallel reviewers to evaluate different aspects: one focusing on methodology and experimental design, the other on novelty and positioning relative to existing work, then bringing them together for a structured discussion to reach consensus.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34391,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34391},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642","uuid":"f6ee964f-105b-4245-984a-be7646ae4e2f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0166T8kmbA7e6cnHEuUcpe9W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Paper read. Now dispatching two parallel reviewers: R1 (Methods + Experiments) and R2 (Novelty + Related Work)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34391,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34391},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642","uuid":"47f2c497-8fa8-4ded-9f51-707be96d3bcb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0166T8kmbA7e6cnHEuUcpe9W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BVRyxqJN2EPHcPpCiYp6P1","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments Review","prompt":"You are **Reviewer 1 (R1)** for a top ML venue review. Your focus: **Methods soundness and Experimental rigor**.\n\nReview standard: top ML venue, acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Structural Self-Consistency for Quality Estimation in LLM-Based Information Extraction\"\n\nThe paper systematically compares 5 unsupervised confidence signals for quality estimation and sample selection in LLM-based structured IE:\n- **Signals:** log-probability (logprob), exact match (EM), Fleiss' κ (FK), Soft Jaccard (SJ), entity voting confidence (Vote)\n- **Tasks:** NER and RE\n- **Models:** Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B (both LoRA fine-tuned)\n- **Datasets:** SciERC, CoNLL-2003 (in-domain); WNUT-2017 (OOD appendix)\n- **Evaluation:** Quality estimation (Spearman ρ, Kendall τ, AUROC) and best-of-N selection (F1)\n\n**3 Main Claims:**\n1. Structural consistency signals (voting, SJ) are strongest unsupervised quality estimators for IE, outperforming logprob by 17–30 AUROC points and 0.2–0.4 in ρ.\n2. A \"correlation–selection gap\" exists: strong instance-level quality prediction doesn't translate to effective best-of-N selection on NER; only logprob enables selection on RE (+2.4pp).\n3. Task-complexity boundary: all signals degrade on RE due to compound error propagation; conditional filtering restores discriminative power.\n\n## Key Experimental Details\n\n**Table 1 (SciERC, Qwen3-8B, N=8):**\n- NER (n=529): Vote ρ=0.502/AUROC=0.728; SJ ρ=0.357/AUROC=0.666; logprob ρ=0.140/AUROC=0.559\n- RE (n=397): Vote ρ=0.422/AUROC=0.716; FK ρ=0.253/AUROC=0.631; logprob ρ=0.247/AUROC=0.635\n\n**Table 2 (2×2 matrix, Spearman ρ, full set, N=8):**\n- All 4 configs: structural > logprob (100% rate)\n- Cross-model Δρ ≤ 0.006 on same dataset\n- Qwen×SciERC: SJ 0.357, Vote 0.502, logprob 0.140\n- Qwen×CoNLL: SJ 0.436, Vote 0.424, logprob 0.316\n- LLaMA×SciERC: SJ 0.363, Vote —, logprob 0.183\n- LLaMA×CoNLL: SJ 0.431, Vote 0.426, logprob 0.307\n\n**Table 3 (AUROC, 2×2 matrix):**\n- 3/4 configs structural leads; exception: LLaMA×CoNLL logprob 0.761 > SJ 0.704\n- Paper explains: high-baseline regime (greedy F1=0.927), logprob well-calibrated for thresholding but ρ still inferior\n\n**Table 4 (3-seed robustness, LLaMA×CoNLL, N=16):**\n- SJ ρ = 0.463±0.008, voting ρ = 0.458±0.003, logprob ρ = 0.310±0.005\n- structural beats logprob rate = 100%\n\n**Table 5 (Best-of-N selection, SciERC):**\n- NER: Oracle 0.769, Greedy 0.609, all signals ≤ 0.609 (no signal beats greedy!)\n- RE: Oracle 0.561, Greedy 0.374, logprob 0.397 (+2.4pp), structural signals ≤ 0.368\n\n**Table 6 (OOD: SciERC→WNUT-2017, Qwen3-8B):**\n- Full set: all ρ near zero; logprob turns negative (−0.031)\n- Conditional: SJ 0.198, Vote 0.224, logprob 0.117\n- Relative signal ordering preserved\n\n**Additional analyses:** Temperature (Δρ ≤ ±0.01 for SJ), ensemble (logistic regression marginal gains), sample budget scaling (n=200 subset, N=8→16 improves RE signals)\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe imagined experiment plan includes:\n1. **exp-011 (ner_ood_robustness):** SciERC→WNUT-17 zero-shot. Expected: greedy F1 drops to 0.143, structural signals weak but positive, logprob goes negative. Paper covers this in Appendix A / Table 6. ✓\n2. **exp-017 (ner_llama_conll):** LLaMA×CoNLL completing the 2×2 matrix + 3-seed robustness. Expected: SJ ρ=0.431, cross-model Δ=0.005. Paper covers in Tables 2, 3, 4. ✓\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\nPlease provide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness**\n   - Are the 5 signals well-defined and fairly compared?\n   - Is the problem formulation (quality estimation vs. sample selection) clean?\n   - Any concerns about the evaluation metrics (ρ, τ, AUROC, best-of-N F1)?\n   - Is the Soft Jaccard metric well-motivated and correctly implemented?\n\n2. **Experimental Rigor**\n   - Is the 2×2 model-dataset matrix sufficient for generalization claims?\n   - Are the sample sizes (n=529, 397, 2756) adequate?\n   - Is the 3-seed robustness analysis on only one configuration (LLaMA×CoNLL) sufficient?\n   - Temperature analysis: only two temperatures (0.7, 1.0) — is this enough?\n   - Sample budget scaling: only n=200 subset — is this a limitation?\n   - OOD experiment: only one direction (SciERC→WNUT) — sufficient?\n\n3. **Statistical Concerns**\n   - Are confidence intervals / significance tests provided?\n   - Bootstrap CIs mentioned?\n   - Multiple comparison corrections?\n\n4. **Experiment Coverage**\n   - Does the paper cover the planned experiments (exp-011, exp-017)?\n   - Any missing experiments that would strengthen claims?\n\n5. **Strengths and Weaknesses** (bulleted)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n\n7. **Preliminary Score** (1-6 scale with justification)\n\nFormat your review as a structured document with clear headers. Be rigorous but fair.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34391,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34391},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642","uuid":"ae2533b8-e217-4f20-bba7-9f14664df6d7"}
