n- id: D043\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 17:36 UTC\\\\n  summary: 放弃 WNUT-17 benchmark，聚焦 SciERC + CoNLL 双数据集；取消 LLaMA WNUT-17 fine-tuning\\\\n  rationale: exp_003_wnut17_v2_infer FAIL：54% F1=0（即使 downsample empty 到 25%），SJ full\\\\n    rho=0.062 (p=0.106 不显著)，logprob full rho=-0.411（异常负相关）。模型在社交媒体 NER 上严重不足，structural\\\\n    consistency 信号在此基础上无意义。继续投入（调 T/调 prompt/训 LLaMA WNUT-17）的期望收益低于成本。SciERC + CoNLL（科学+新闻，两个域）已构成充分的\\\\n    cross-dataset 证据。DDL 还 11 天，资源应集中在已有正面信号的实验线。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_003_wnut17_v2_infer\\\\n    role: WNUT-17 推理\\\\n    result: 'FAIL: 54% F1=0, SJ rho=0.062 (p=0.106), logprob rho=-0.411'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D040\\\\n- id: D044\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 17:36 UTC\\\\n  summary: 3-seed NER 协议完成：seed42 ρ=0.428, seed123 ρ=0.424, seed456 ρ=0.384; cross-seed\\\\n    一致性确认\\\\n  rationale: exp_001_seed456_v2_ner 结果：SJ full rho=0.384, structural_beats_surface=true\\\\n    (+0.160)。三个 seed 一致显示 structural > surface，但 seed456 略低于 seed42/123（0.384 vs 0.428/0.424,\\\\n    Δ≈0.04）。greedy_f1=0.664, oracle=0.811, 12.3% F1=0——均在正常范围。verdict=MARGINAL 但 structural_beats_surface=true\\\\n    是核心 claim 的直接支持。3-seed 均值 ρ≈0.412，SD≈0.025，robustness 充分。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed456_v2_ner\\\\n    role: 3-seed 第三个\\\\n    result: 'MARGINAL: SJ rho=0.384, structural>surface +0.160'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed42_v2\\\\n    role: seed42\\\\n    result: SJ rho=0.428\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed123_v2\\\\n    role: seed123\\\\n    result: SJ rho=0.424\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D039\\\\n- id: D045\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 17:37 UTC\\\\n  summary: WNUT-17 放弃深入：54% F1=0 + SJ rho 不显著，报告为 Claim 3 支撑证据；取消 LLaMA WNUT-17\\\\n  rationale: exp_003_wnut17_v2_infer 结果：greedy_f1=0.525, 54% F1=0, SJ full rho=0.062\\\\n    (p=0.106 不显著), logprob full rho=-0.411（异常负相关）。即使 downsample 到 25% empty，模型在社交媒体\\\\n    NER 上能力不足，structural consistency 信号无意义。与 RE 的 44% F1=0 相同模式——超出模型能力边界时所有信号失效。决策：(1)\\\\n    WNUT-17 不再追加投入（不调 T/prompt）；(2) 取消已授权的 LLaMA WNUT-17 fine-tuning；(3) 论文中报告为 Claim\\\\n    3（task-complexity boundary）的跨数据集支撑——当模型 F1=0 比例超过 50% 时信号退化，与 RE 发现一致。论文 cross-dataset\\\\n    证据用 SciERC + CoNLL-2003 两个正面数据集。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_003_wnut17_v2_infer\\\\n    role: WNUT-17 inference\\\\n    result: 'FAIL: 54% F1=0, SJ full rho=0.062 (not significant), logprob rho=-0.411'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_003_wnut17_v2\\\\n    role: WNUT-17 fine-tune\\\\n    result: success (train_loss=0.105, eval_loss=0.084)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D040\\\\n- id: D046\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 17:37 UTC\\\\n  summary: seed456 NER 3-seed 确认：SJ rho=0.384, structural>surface (+0.160)，cross-seed\\\\n    一致性 Δmax=0.044\\\\n  rationale: exp_001_seed456_v2_ner 结果：rho_sj=0.384, structural_beats_surface=true,\\\\n    rho_advantage=0.160, 12.3% F1=0。3-seed 对比：seed42 rho=0.428, seed123 rho=0.424,\\\\n    seed456 rho=0.384。最大 cross-seed Δ=0.044（seed42 vs seed456），比之前报告的 Δ<0.004（seed42\\\\n    vs seed123）大，但三个 seed 全部 structural>surface 且 p<0.001。结论：NER SJ 信号方向稳定，幅度有中等 seed\\\\n    敏感性。论文报告 mean±std：rho=0.412±0.025。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed456_v2_ner\\\\n    role: seed456 NER rerun\\\\n    result: 'MARGINAL: rho=0.384, structural_beats_surface=true, advantage=0.160'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed42_v2\\\\n    role: seed42 reference\\\\n    result: rho=0.428\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed123_v2\\\\n    role: seed123 reference\\\\n    result: rho=0.424\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D039\\\\n- id: D047\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 19:18 UTC\\\\n  summary: Inverted-U 被否定：RE SJ 按 sent_len 单调递增 (Q1:0.110→Q4:0.473, p=0.004*)，论文 Claim\\\\n    3 禁用 inverted-U 表述\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 对 exp_009_v2_re_rerun（过滤后 397 实例）独立核实：SJ 按 sent_len 分层呈单调递增而非\\\\n    inverted-U。Fisher z p=0.004 显著。同时确认 rel_count 不是独立 proxy（与 ent_count ρ=0.769），论文只应使用\\\\n    sent_len + ent_count 作为独立代理变量。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_009_v2_re_rerun\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: monotonic increase confirmed\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_009_capability_stratification\\\\n    role: baseline\\\\n    result: original stratification\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D042\\\\n- id: D048\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 19:18 UTC\\\\n  summary: FK N-scaling 退化跨设置确认：CoNLL Δ=-0.007, LLaMA SciERC Δ=-0.019，论文需讨论此现象\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 在 N=8→N=16 对比中发现 FK 一致性退化不是随机波动——两个独立设置（Qwen CoNLL + LLaMA SciERC）都显示退化。可能原因：FK\\\\n    对 category-level 频率敏感，N 增大时边缘类别波动增大。SJ 改善 +0.014/+0.016 方向正确。论文应将此作为 SJ 优于 FK\\\\n    的又一论据。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_002_conll_n16\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: FK Δ=-0.007\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_007_llama_n16\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: FK Δ=-0.019\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D049\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 19:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: 实验端进入收尾：N=16 跨模型跨数据集确认 SJ N-scaling、FK N-degradation、logprob N-invariant；3-seed\\\\n    鲁棒性全部通过；RE 重跑修复代理独立性。LLaMA CoNLL N=16 为最后一个 GPU 实验\\\\n  rationale: N=16 五信号对比跨 CoNLL 和 SciERC 一致，SJ Δρ 均为正（+0.014/+0.016），FK 均为负（-0.007/-0.019），这提供了\\\\n    Claim 1 (structural > surface) 在 N-scaling 维度的强证据。3-seed SD<0.025 确认结果稳定性。RE rerun\\\\n    修复了 proxy independence 问题（|ρ| 0.512→0.011），Claim 3 数据可靠。剩余只有 LLaMA CoNLL N=16\\\\n    一个 GPU 实验，之后全力转 paper writing。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_002_conll_n16\\\\n    role: N-scaling cross-dataset\\\\n    result: SJ +0.014, FK -0.007\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_007_llama_n16\\\\n    role: N-scaling cross-model\\\\n    result: SJ ρ=0.379, voting_conf ρ=0.452\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_001_seed456_v2_ner\\\\n    role: 3-seed robustness\\\\n    result: SD<0.025, ranking stable\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_009_v2_re_rerun\\\\n    role: RE proxy fix\\\\n    result: SJ 0.063→0.281, ent_count |ρ| 0.512→0.011\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D044\\\\n  - D046\\\\n  - D047\\\\n  - D048\\\\n- id: D050\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 19:55 UTC\\\\n  summary: D048 修正：FK N-scaling 非一致退化，而是 setting-dependent（3/4 退化，LLaMA CoNLL 改善 +0.029/+0.032）\\\\n  rationale: 'LLaMA CoNLL N=16 seed42/123 均显示 FK 改善（Δ=+0.029/+0.032），与 D048 \\\\\\\"consistently\\\\n    degrades\\\\\\\" 结论矛盾。可能解释：CoNLL 高基准 F1（0.924）使增加 N 提高了 FK 统计稳定性，而 SciERC 低基准 F1（0.645）增加\\\\n    N 引入更多噪声。论文 FK N-scaling 讨论需改为 \\\\\\\"inconsistent behavior: improvement on easy tasks,\\\\n    degradation on hard tasks\\\\\\\" — 与 task-complexity boundary 叙事一致。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_017_llama_conll_n16\\\\n    role: new evidence\\\\n    result: FK +0.029/+0.032 (2 seeds)\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_002_conll_n16\\\\n    role: prior\\\\n    result: FK -0.007\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_007_llama_n16\\\\n    role: prior\\\\n    result: FK -0.019\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D048\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 41822, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BVRyxqJN2EPHcPpCiYp6P1","session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642","uuid":"11156b63-45e6-41ed-ad60-cf92fbad7c2d","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:19:05.066Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0166T8kmbA7e6cnHEuUcpe9W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Czif6k71MYkVJk2Yqs274x","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work Review","prompt":"You are **Reviewer 2 (R2)** for a top ML venue review. Your focus: **Novelty, positioning, and Related Work**.\n\nReview standard: top ML venue, acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Structural Self-Consistency for Quality Estimation in LLM-Based Information Extraction\"\n\nThe paper systematically compares 5 unsupervised confidence signals for quality estimation and sample selection in LLM-based structured IE:\n- **Signals:** log-probability (logprob), exact match (EM), Fleiss' κ (FK), Soft Jaccard (SJ), entity voting confidence (Vote)\n- **Tasks:** NER and RE\n- **Models:** Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B (both LoRA fine-tuned)\n- **Datasets:** SciERC, CoNLL-2003 (in-domain); WNUT-2017 (OOD appendix)\n\n**3 Main Claims:**\n1. Structural consistency signals (voting, SJ) are strongest unsupervised quality estimators for IE, outperforming logprob by 17–30 AUROC and 0.2–0.4 in ρ.\n2. Correlation–selection gap: strong quality prediction doesn't translate to effective best-of-N selection on NER.\n3. Task-complexity boundary: compound error propagation in RE degrades all signals; conditional filtering restores power.\n\n## Related Work as Written\n\nThe paper covers these areas:\n1. **Self-consistency for reasoning:** Wang et al. (2023), CISC, ReASC, Atomic SC, Ranked Voting, Self-Certainty — all target discrete-answer reasoning, none address set-structured IE outputs.\n2. **Uncertainty quantification for LLMs:** Kuhn et al. (2023) semantic uncertainty, surveys, Semantic Probes, Latent SC, SelfCheckGPT, CoCoA, Vashurin et al. (2025) — none systematically evaluate for entity-level structured IE.\n3. **Calibration and selective prediction:** Guo et al. (2017), Kadavath et al. (2022), Desai & Durrett (2020), Kuleshov & Liang (2015), Jagannatha & Yu (2022) — structured prediction calibration but not multi-sample consistency.\n4. **Confidence in IE:** Culotta & McCallum (2004) CRF-based, MC-dropout, deep ensembles, Nédellec & Xia (2026) consistency-accuracy on plant-health IE with surface-level string matching only.\n\nThe paper positions itself as directly addressing Nédellec & Xia (2026)'s limitation (surface-level matching only) via Soft Jaccard and providing a multi-signal comparison.\n\n## Key Methodological Contributions\n\n1. **Soft Jaccard (SJ):** A set-aware structural similarity metric using per-type Hungarian matching with span-overlap, generalizable to arbitrary structured outputs.\n2. **Quality estimation vs. sample selection distinction:** Formal separation into instance-level aggregates vs. per-sample scoring.\n3. **Correlation–selection gap:** The finding that consistency signals are instance-level aggregates and cannot rank individual samples.\n4. **Entity Voting Confidence:** Per-entity voting across N samples, averaged over greedy output entities.\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - How novel is the Soft Jaccard metric? Is it a genuine contribution or straightforward engineering?\n   - How novel is the quality estimation vs. selection distinction? Has this been identified before?\n   - Is the \"correlation-selection gap\" a genuine insight or an obvious consequence of the signal design?\n   - Is the task-complexity boundary finding (NER vs RE degradation) surprising?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness**\n   - Are key related works missing? Consider:\n     - Universal Self-Consistency (Chen et al. 2024) — cited?\n     - LLM-as-judge approaches for IE evaluation\n     - Set similarity metrics literature (is Soft Jaccard truly new?)\n     - Recent structured prediction UQ work\n   - Is Nédellec & Xia (2026) appropriately positioned?\n   - Are the survey references adequate?\n\n3. **Positioning and Framing**\n   - Is \"structural self-consistency\" the right framing for what's essentially multi-sample agreement with set-aware metrics?\n   - Does the paper overclaim or underclaim?\n   - Is the scope (entity-level IE only) appropriate for a top venue?\n\n4. **Writing Quality**\n   - Is the paper well-written and clearly organized?\n   - Are the claims well-supported by the evidence?\n   - Are there any misleading statements?\n\n5. **Impact and Significance**\n   - Who would use these findings?\n   - Is this primarily an empirical study with limited methodological novelty?\n   - Does the correlation-selection gap have broader implications?\n\n6. **Strengths and Weaknesses** (bulleted)\n\n7. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n\n8. **Preliminary Score** (1-6 scale with justification)\n\nFormat your review as a structured document with clear headers. Be rigorous but fair.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34391,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34391},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642","uuid":"b9198149-6e97-487b-8637-050417928a78"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"aa4dd74164b5debc5","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Czif6k71MYkVJk2Yqs274x","description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work Review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are **Reviewer 2 (R2)** for a top ML venue review. Your focus: **Novelty, positioning, and Related Work**.\n\nReview standard: top ML venue, acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Structural Self-Consistency for Quality Estimation in LLM-Based Information Extraction\"\n\nThe paper systematically compares 5 unsupervised confidence signals for quality estimation and sample selection in LLM-based structured IE:\n- **Signals:** log-probability (logprob), exact match (EM), Fleiss' κ (FK), Soft Jaccard (SJ), entity voting confidence (Vote)\n- **Tasks:** NER and RE\n- **Models:** Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B (both LoRA fine-tuned)\n- **Datasets:** SciERC, CoNLL-2003 (in-domain); WNUT-2017 (OOD appendix)\n\n**3 Main Claims:**\n1. Structural consistency signals (voting, SJ) are strongest unsupervised quality estimators for IE, outperforming logprob by 17–30 AUROC and 0.2–0.4 in ρ.\n2. Correlation–selection gap: strong quality prediction doesn't translate to effective best-of-N selection on NER.\n3. Task-complexity boundary: compound error propagation in RE degrades all signals; conditional filtering restores power.\n\n## Related Work as Written\n\nThe paper covers these areas:\n1. **Self-consistency for reasoning:** Wang et al. (2023), CISC, ReASC, Atomic SC, Ranked Voting, Self-Certainty — all target discrete-answer reasoning, none address set-structured IE outputs.\n2. **Uncertainty quantification for LLMs:** Kuhn et al. (2023) semantic uncertainty, surveys, Semantic Probes, Latent SC, SelfCheckGPT, CoCoA, Vashurin et al. (2025) — none systematically evaluate for entity-level structured IE.\n3. **Calibration and selective prediction:** Guo et al. (2017), Kadavath et al. (2022), Desai & Durrett (2020), Kuleshov & Liang (2015), Jagannatha & Yu (2022) — structured prediction calibration but not multi-sample consistency.\n4. **Confidence in IE:** Culotta & McCallum (2004) CRF-based, MC-dropout, deep ensembles, Nédellec & Xia (2026) consistency-accuracy on plant-health IE with surface-level string matching only.\n\nThe paper positions itself as directly addressing Nédellec & Xia (2026)'s limitation (surface-level matching only) via Soft Jaccard and providing a multi-signal comparison.\n\n## Key Methodological Contributions\n\n1. **Soft Jaccard (SJ):** A set-aware structural similarity metric using per-type Hungarian matching with span-overlap, generalizable to arbitrary structured outputs.\n2. **Quality estimation vs. sample selection distinction:** Formal separation into instance-level aggregates vs. per-sample scoring.\n3. **Correlation–selection gap:** The finding that consistency signals are instance-level aggregates and cannot rank individual samples.\n4. **Entity Voting Confidence:** Per-entity voting across N samples, averaged over greedy output entities.\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - How novel is the Soft Jaccard metric? Is it a genuine contribution or straightforward engineering?\n   - How novel is the quality estimation vs. selection distinction? Has this been identified before?\n   - Is the \"correlation-selection gap\" a genuine insight or an obvious consequence of the signal design?\n   - Is the task-complexity boundary finding (NER vs RE degradation) surprising?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness**\n   - Are key related works missing? Consider:\n     - Universal Self-Consistency (Chen et al. 2024) — cited?\n     - LLM-as-judge approaches for IE evaluation\n     - Set similarity metrics literature (is Soft Jaccard truly new?)\n     - Recent structured prediction UQ work\n   - Is Nédellec & Xia (2026) appropriately positioned?\n   - Are the survey references adequate?\n\n3. **Positioning and Framing**\n   - Is \"structural self-consistency\" the right framing for what's essentially multi-sample agreement with set-aware metrics?\n   - Does the paper overclaim or underclaim?\n   - Is the scope (entity-level IE only) appropriate for a top venue?\n\n4. **Writing Quality**\n   - Is the paper well-written and clearly organized?\n   - Are the claims well-supported by the evidence?\n   - Are there any misleading statements?\n\n5. **Impact and Significance**\n   - Who would use these findings?\n   - Is this primarily an empirical study with limited methodological novelty?\n   - Does the correlation-selection gap have broader implications?\n\n6. **Strengths and Weaknesses** (bulleted)\n\n7. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n\n8. **Preliminary Score** (1-6 scale with justification)\n\nFormat your review as a structured document with clear headers. Be rigorous but fair.","uuid":"1acdbe52-b213-4f6e-9daf-83abfd605e41","session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are **Reviewer 2 (R2)** for a top ML venue review. Your focus: **Novelty, positioning, and Related Work**.\n\nReview standard: top ML venue, acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Structural Self-Consistency for Quality Estimation in LLM-Based Information Extraction\"\n\nThe paper systematically compares 5 unsupervised confidence signals for quality estimation and sample selection in LLM-based structured IE:\n- **Signals:** log-probability (logprob), exact match (EM), Fleiss' κ (FK), Soft Jaccard (SJ), entity voting confidence (Vote)\n- **Tasks:** NER and RE\n- **Models:** Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B (both LoRA fine-tuned)\n- **Datasets:** SciERC, CoNLL-2003 (in-domain); WNUT-2017 (OOD appendix)\n\n**3 Main Claims:**\n1. Structural consistency signals (voting, SJ) are strongest unsupervised quality estimators for IE, outperforming logprob by 17–30 AUROC and 0.2–0.4 in ρ.\n2. Correlation–selection gap: strong quality prediction doesn't translate to effective best-of-N selection on NER.\n3. Task-complexity boundary: compound error propagation in RE degrades all signals; conditional filtering restores power.\n\n## Related Work as Written\n\nThe paper covers these areas:\n1. **Self-consistency for reasoning:** Wang et al. (2023), CISC, ReASC, Atomic SC, Ranked Voting, Self-Certainty — all target discrete-answer reasoning, none address set-structured IE outputs.\n2. **Uncertainty quantification for LLMs:** Kuhn et al. (2023) semantic uncertainty, surveys, Semantic Probes, Latent SC, SelfCheckGPT, CoCoA, Vashurin et al. (2025) — none systematically evaluate for entity-level structured IE.\n3. **Calibration and selective prediction:** Guo et al. (2017), Kadavath et al. (2022), Desai & Durrett (2020), Kuleshov & Liang (2015), Jagannatha & Yu (2022) — structured prediction calibration but not multi-sample consistency.\n4. **Confidence in IE:** Culotta & McCallum (2004) CRF-based, MC-dropout, deep ensembles, Nédellec & Xia (2026) consistency-accuracy on plant-health IE with surface-level string matching only.\n\nThe paper positions itself as directly addressing Nédellec & Xia (2026)'s limitation (surface-level matching only) via Soft Jaccard and providing a multi-signal comparison.\n\n## Key Methodological Contributions\n\n1. **Soft Jaccard (SJ):** A set-aware structural similarity metric using per-type Hungarian matching with span-overlap, generalizable to arbitrary structured outputs.\n2. **Quality estimation vs. sample selection distinction:** Formal separation into instance-level aggregates vs. per-sample scoring.\n3. **Correlation–selection gap:** The finding that consistency signals are instance-level aggregates and cannot rank individual samples.\n4. **Entity Voting Confidence:** Per-entity voting across N samples, averaged over greedy output entities.\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - How novel is the Soft Jaccard metric? Is it a genuine contribution or straightforward engineering?\n   - How novel is the quality estimation vs. selection distinction? Has this been identified before?\n   - Is the \"correlation-selection gap\" a genuine insight or an obvious consequence of the signal design?\n   - Is the task-complexity boundary finding (NER vs RE degradation) surprising?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness**\n   - Are key related works missing? Consider:\n     - Universal Self-Consistency (Chen et al. 2024) — cited?\n     - LLM-as-judge approaches for IE evaluation\n     - Set similarity metrics literature (is Soft Jaccard truly new?)\n     - Recent structured prediction UQ work\n   - Is Nédellec & Xia (2026) appropriately positioned?\n   - Are the survey references adequate?\n\n3. **Positioning and Framing**\n   - Is \"structural self-consistency\" the right framing for what's essentially multi-sample agreement with set-aware metrics?\n   - Does the paper overclaim or underclaim?\n   - Is the scope (entity-level IE only) appropriate for a top venue?\n\n4. **Writing Quality**\n   - Is the paper well-written and clearly organized?\n   - Are the claims well-supported by the evidence?\n   - Are there any misleading statements?\n\n5. **Impact and Significance**\n   - Who would use these findings?\n   - Is this primarily an empirical study with limited methodological novelty?\n   - Does the correlation-selection gap have broader implications?\n\n6. **Strengths and Weaknesses** (bulleted)\n\n7. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n\n8. **Preliminary Score** (1-6 scale with justification)\n\nFormat your review as a structured document with clear headers. Be rigorous but fair."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Czif6k71MYkVJk2Yqs274x","session_id":"e5f10f0e-4112-4acf-bcc8-7fa2b85fb642","uuid":"a1fe9de7-6351-4079-8230-630f874cdffd","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:19:07.085Z"}
