nformal prediction to few-shot settings via meta-learning over auxiliary tasks, producing tighter\\\\n      prediction sets with formal coverage guarantees. SUPPLEMENTARY - CP not a method component, angelopoulos2021 retained as main CP reference.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  angelopoulos2021conformal:\\\\n    title: Uncertainty Sets for Image Classifiers using Conformal Prediction\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Anastasios N. Angelopoulos\\\\n    - Stephen Bates\\\\n    - Jitendra Malik\\\\n    - Michael I. Jordan\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2021\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.14193\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: angelopoulos2021conformal\\\\n    category: conformal_prediction\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Introduces RAPS (Regularized Adaptive Prediction Sets) with finite-sample coverage guarantees. Foundation for\\\\n      conformal prediction methodology we adapt to structured IE output sets.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  bates2021rcps:\\\\n    title: Distribution-Free, Risk-Controlling Prediction Sets\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Stephen Bates\\\\n    - Anastasios Angelopoulos\\\\n    - Lihua Lei\\\\n    - Jitendra Malik\\\\n    - Michael I. Jordan\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: Journal of the ACM 2021\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02703\\\\n    doi: 10.1145/3478535\\\\n    bibtex_key: bates2021rcps\\\\n    category: conformal_prediction\\\\n    role: supplementary\\\\n    relevance: 'Generalizes conformal prediction to control arbitrary monotone losses for set-valued predictors with finite-sample\\\\n      guarantees. SUPPLEMENTARY - CP not a method component, angelopoulos2021 retained as main CP reference.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  xiao2019uncertainty:\\\\n    title: Quantifying Uncertainties in Natural Language Processing Tasks\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Yijun Xiao\\\\n    - William Yang Wang\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    venue: AAAI 2019\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.07253\\\\n    doi: 10.1609/aaai.v33i01.33017322\\\\n    bibtex_key: xiao2019uncertainty\\\\n    category: token_span_uncertainty_ner\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Pioneers Bayesian uncertainty quantification for NLP tasks including NER, showing that modeling data and model\\\\n      uncertainty improves both performance and reliability for token-level predictions.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  shelmanov2021active:\\\\n    title: Active Learning for Sequence Tagging with Deep Pre-trained Models and Bayesian Uncertainty Estimates\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Artem Shelmanov\\\\n    - Dmitri Puzyrev\\\\n    - Lyubov Kupriyanova\\\\n    - Denis Belyakov\\\\n    - Daniil Larionov\\\\n    - Nikita Khromov\\\\n    - Olga Kozlova\\\\n    - Ekaterina Artemova\\\\n    - Dmitry V. Dylov\\\\n    - Alexander Panchenko\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: EACL 2021\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.08133\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2021.eacl-main.145\\\\n    bibtex_key: shelmanov2021active\\\\n    category: token_span_uncertainty_ner\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Extensive empirical study of Bayesian uncertainty estimation (MC dropout variants) for sequence tagging with\\\\n      pre-trained models. Establishes best practices for uncertainty-guided active learning in NER.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'